%% One valuation run, in order, with the real operations named.
%% Note: avoid "->", angle brackets and semicolons in message text. The
%% lexer reads them as arrow tokens and fails to parse.
sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  participant MD as market_data.json
  participant B as bootstrap
  participant QL as GlobalBootstrap
  participant SC as coeffs
  participant GPU as CUDA device
  participant V as reconcile

  MD->>B: 14 curves of tagged quotes

  Note over B: build order is forced, not arbitrary:<br/>ESTR ECB before EURIBOR, AONIA RBA before BBSW,<br/>SOFR before the two FX curves. The BBSW pair is a<br/>staged joint solve on the 3s6s basis, and the CTD<br/>curve is derived last from SOFR and both FX curves

  loop per curve, in dependency order
    B->>B: quote to RateHelper by type
    alt dual-curve or cross-currency
      B->>B: attach the already-built foreign curve<br/>ESTR ECB discounts EURIBOR, SOFR is the USD leg
      B->>QL: FxSwap and XccyBasis helpers, two curves in play
      QL-->>B: EUR curve implied under USD collateral
    else single currency
      B->>QL: all helpers for the curve
      QL-->>B: term structure
    end
    Note over QL: all n pillars solved at once,<br/>so a quote is repriced by the same<br/>finished curve it helped build
  end

  B->>SC: calibrated term structures
  loop per pillar interval
    SC->>SC: read the coefficients the curve holds
  end
  SC->>GPU: cudaMemcpy coefficient array
  Note over SC,GPU: the device is sent what the curve<br/>is already made of, so nothing is<br/>approximated on the way across

  par CPU reference path
    B->>V: prices, PV01 re-bootstrapped per bump
  and GPU path
    GPU->>GPU: binary search, then Horner
    GPU->>V: device prices, pillar ladder
  end

  V->>V: difference both paths, 348 instruments
  V-->>MD: worst agreement 5.4e-14
